  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There is an array of NNN integers, and a range [L,R][L, R][L,R].\n\nLet f(A)=∏1≤i&lt;j≤N(Ai⊕Aj)f(A) = \\prod_{1 \\le i &lt; j \\le N} (A_i \\oplus A_j)f(A)=∏1≤i&lt;j≤N​(Ai​⊕Aj​). Informally, f(A)f(A)f(A) is the product of all pairwise XOR's of the array AAA.\n\nIf the resulting value lies between LLL and RRR (both inclusive), we call such an array a **Halloween array**.\n\nGiven an array, determine whether it is a **Halloween array** or not. Print YES\\text{YES}YES or NO\\text{NO}NO accordingly.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of input contains NNN, LLL and RRR - the size of the array, and the left and right bounds of the interval respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers - A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput on a new line YES\\text{YES}YES if the array is a halloween array else NO\\text{NO}NO.\n\n\nIt is allowed to output each character in either case. yes\\text{yes}yes, YeS\\text{YeS}YeS will also be considered as a positive response.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤1090 \\le A_i \\le 10^90≤Ai​≤109",
      "0≤L≤R≤1090 \\le L \\le R \\le 10^90≤L≤R≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
